# config.local.env — machine-local overrides. NOT tracked by git.
#
# This file is auto-seeded from config.local.env.example on first run of any
# script (build/run/status/stop), then sourced after config.env — so anything
# set here overrides the tracked defaults and stays on this machine only.

# Extra apt system libraries, space-separated. Reinstalled by entrypoint.sh on
# every container start, so they persist across restarts without an image
# rebuild. The .deb downloads are cached in the named volume ds-apt-cache-<profile>,
# so re-installs after the first pull are fast/offline.
#
# Per-profile: APT_PACKAGES_A / APT_PACKAGES_B apply to that profile only.
# APT_PACKAGES (no suffix) is a shared fallback used when the per-profile var is
# unset. A per-profile value fully replaces the fallback (they are not merged).
#
# Empty by default (fresh machines install nothing). Add libs here, e.g.:
#   APT_PACKAGES_A="libmagick++-dev libv8-dev"
# Or just `apt install <pkg>` inside the container — the apt wrapper appends it
# to the matching line below automatically (disable with APT_AUTOSAVE=false).
#
# Prefer conda-forge (micromamba install -n denv -c conda-forge <lib>) when a
# build exists; once your list is stable, bake it into the Containerfile apt layer.
APT_PACKAGES_A=""
APT_PACKAGES_B=""
# APT_PACKAGES="shared-lib-for-all-profiles"

# Extra bind mounts passed to every service container (run.sh appends them to
# the podman run args). Word-split on spaces — no spaces within individual
# values. Setting this here overrides any EXTRA_VOLUMES exported by the login
# environment (e.g. the ansible-rendered per-user default for supplementary
# disks), so include those mounts too if you add your own.
# EXTRA_VOLUMES="-v /mnt/disks/<disk>:/mnt/disks/<disk>:Z"

# Max memory per service container (podman --memory). Overrides the tracked
# CONTAINER_MEMORY=auto default in config.env ("auto" = system RAM minus 2G).
# Always capped at total-2G; a per-launch --memory / -m flag beats this value.
# CONTAINER_MEMORY=16G

# ---- Extra / lightweight profiles (user-definable, no root needed) ----
# Profiles beyond A/B are defined entirely here — no admin or image-script edit.
# Each needs at least R_VERSION_<X> and PYTHON_VERSION_<X>; ports default to
# "auto" (first free in 8901-8920). Launch with `<service> -p <x>` (e.g.
# `rstudio -p c`) or `./run.sh <x> <service>`. If the resulting image tag
# already exists (e.g. same versions as profile A) no build is needed; otherwise
# run `build <x>` (or `./build.sh <x>`) once first.
#
#   R_VERSION_C=4.4.3
#   PYTHON_VERSION_C=3.12
#   JUPYTER_PORT_C=auto
#   RSTUDIO_PORT_C=auto
#   VSCODE_PORT_C=auto
#
# LIGHTWEIGHT_<X>=true builds/uses a stripped image (ds-env-lite-*): only R +
# Python + the IDE machinery (JupyterLab/ipykernel, IRkernel + R languageserver,
# code-server, Claude Code) + gcloud SDK — NO CUDA, PyTorch, numpy/pandas/
# matplotlib/scikit-learn, or tidyverse/Seurat/Bioconductor. rstudio/jupyter/
# vscode all still work; the image is fast to build and small. Always needs a
# one-time `build <x>` unless the baked shared store already prebuilt it at
# these versions.
#
#   R_VERSION_D=4.4.3
#   PYTHON_VERSION_D=3.12
#   LIGHTWEIGHT_D=true
